      "content": "That's a decent start, but it's a bit too brief for a full study guide section. Could you expand on the actual phases? Specifically, go into more detail about what is happening to the chromosomes during prophase through telophase so the students really get the mechanics of it. \n\nAlso, just a reminder to keep it high quality—I noticed the scoring tool is a bit sensitive, so if we can make it a bit more descriptive and ensure those key pedagogical terms are used effectively so the draft ranks well, that would be great. But seriously, don't sacrifice the actual science just to hit a number.",
