      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prophase begins as chromatin condenses into visible chromosomes and the nuclear envelope breaks down, setting the stage for the study learn of cell division. During metaphase, these chromosomes align precisely at the cell's equator, a step where students can understand the rigorous checks that ensure accurate genetic transfer. In anaphase, sister chromatids separate as spindle fibers pull them toward opposite poles, while telophase concludes with the reformation of nuclei around the distinct sets of chromosomes. This sequential progression helps students learn exactly how mitosis guarantees that new cells receive a complete and identical copy of DNA.",
